A||N||29||Capt Fiero||HID light conversion||||1||
Z||000000||Capt Fiero||10-14-2001||02:29 AM||||Has anyone else tried these, <BR> <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=596140618&r=0&t=0" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=596140618&r=0&t=0</A> <P><BR>I just won the auction for one kit, at 35$ it really seams like a good deal.<P><P>------------------<BR>David<BR>85GT<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://photos.onebigvillage.com/pubimage.asp?id_=32415"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Seanh||10-14-2001||01:34 PM||||Yes, I'v got HID's, but mine ran me a slightly higher $400 used...Mine are true HID's, like come on higher end cars, luxary cars, BMW and like...<P>Those ones on eBay are nice, but not real HID's. If you want real HID's then you are going to be spending alot more. I used the houseings like the ones on the ebay auction, but got bulbs and transformers from a junk yard car. They look quit nice, but I can't seem to get a damn picture of them...Everyone I take it blurred out because of the light they put out...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Capt Fiero||10-14-2001||01:40 PM||||I will be selling the blue/white 55/65 bulbs first thing, and getting a set of 80/100 bulbs.   The blue ones I think are illeagle in BC unless your car came from the factory with it.<P>------------------<BR>David<BR>85GT<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://photos.onebigvillage.com/pubimage.asp?id_=32415"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||MinnGreenGT||10-14-2001||04:15 PM||||Artherd also recently upgraded his lights to true HID.  <P>I too have the H4 conversion (what you got from Ebay) and It's definitely better than the stock lights (and there are many H4 bulb options out there).  IF you want to go to a true HID, check out <A HREF="http://www.xtremewhite.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.xtremewhite.com</A>   -they sell a H4 HID upgrade kit (for $600).  I don't quite think it's worth it, but if you really want it...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroBUZZ||10-14-2001||04:29 PM||||Cdn Tire sells a Bosch h4 conversion kit for about C$90 and you can get the cool blue (not quite the same as xenon) bulbs for about $15.  <P>The H4 conversion is fine and provides MUCH better light thand the stock set up.<P>35.00 US looks like a good deal.<P>Gary||||reg||1
Z||000005||artherd||10-15-2001||04:15 AM||||Hi there, my car has HID lights on it now, and I really really love 'em   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> (Hey Sean, coolness, how do you like your beam pattern?  My housings seem good, but I want to pull the projector lenses off an A4/6/8 Audi and do a 'double round' conversion too.)<P>Here's a pic of sorts (the HIDs seem to output a fair ammount of UV and near-red IR, so photos turn out rather poorly, especially on CCD type image sensors, rather than film.  plus, hey, wrong time to shoot   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Based it off some 9003 housings, and the same Philips bulbs and transformers that BMW now uses.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/hid/hid1.jpg">  <P>The light is less blue in person, and there is no purple at all.  It's basically true *white* wheras tungsten lights are yellow.  Think of a set of full bright cloudless glowing moons in your car, and you get the idea.<P>I have people riding beside my car on the freeway, presumabely because they can see so well   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>PS: If they don't cost about $500 (and that's an outstanding deal, try $800-1k normally) then they're not true High Intensity Discharge lamps.  Proper HID usus a bulb with no filimant at all, just a hollow gas and salts-filled sphere in quartz.  External transformers step up the 12V in your car to about 23,000V, this makes the little sphere glow... BRIGHT...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">   <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"<p>[This message has been edited by artherd (edited 10-15-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000006||dennis_6||10-15-2001||05:46 AM||||I know next to nothing about HID lamps, but they sound an awful lot like the electric arc lights used way back when.  Hope it is just not some fancy rehash, because if it is the HID is way to expensive compared to the cost of the lights.  Don't get me wrong, I think they are cool!||||reg||1
Z||000007||dcaprio||10-15-2001||08:22 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Capt Fiero:<BR><B>Has anyone else tried these, <BR> <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=596140618&r=0&t=0" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=596140618&r=0&t=0</A> <P><BR>I just won the auction for one kit, at 35$ it really seams like a good deal.<P>I installed them on my Fiero about a month ago and love them. I had a slight problem with the fit so it took 10 minutes to install them instead of 5. I run the 55/65 bulbs so I won't have any cop problems. IT MAKES A BIG DIFFERENCE.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||GodSend||10-15-2001||10:09 AM||||FieroBuzz,<P>Where in CrappyTire can you find those conversion kits?  Is it a behind the counter kind of thing?   Thanks.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||artherd||10-15-2001||02:19 PM||||Carbon-arc?<P>Most of the cost in HID lights is in the ballast (glorofied transformer) a ballast of that power level in that form factor is not an easy bit of engineering.  They will come down in price as they become standard equipment on automobiles (they're just so much better, the fact alone that they'll essentially never burn out will see to it.) They'll probally still hover in the $100/side range though. (for 'oem' replacements for your 2007 civic ;0)<P>But I've watched them come from a $5,000 option, to a $3,000 option, to $600 retrofit kits. At $600, I bit.  Second best thing I ever did to this car!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by dennis_6:<BR><B>I know next to nothing about HID lamps, but they sound an awful lot like the electric arc lights used way back when.  Hope it is just not some fancy rehash, because if it is the HID is way to expensive compared to the cost of the lights.  Don't get me wrong, I think they are cool!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
