Z||000013||FieroBUZZ||10-16-2001||06:49 AM||||Godsend, you have mail.<P>Gary||||reg||1
Z||000014||artherd||10-16-2001||04:24 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by birdpoo:<BR><B>very nice artherd. are there any legalities concerning hid lights for our cars? (calif)</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'm not aware of any as such, I'd say from the volume of HID equiped cars in CA, that they're simply here to stay.   <P>People who don't know what the Fiero is keep saying "woah, you have one of those nice brand new cars with the good headlights"<P>Heh, people think they're OE (one who though that the Fiero is a 2003 car that hasn't been offically introduced yet...)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">   <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"<p>[This message has been edited by artherd (edited 10-16-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000015||lowCG||10-17-2001||09:20 PM||||Now that's pretty cool.<BR>I can remember the difference when I installed the 9003 bulbs that I believe the Ogre recomended here on the forum,with the bulbs rotated sideways for a flatter beam.<P>Those HIDs must be very,very nice indeed.<P>The old Lexus just got a set of PIAA super white,zenon replacement bulbs;not a whole heck of a lot of difference there,a little though.Maybe the Fiero will get the real thing when I can find a set in the boneyard.||||reg||1
