Z||000027||TRiAD||10-21-2001||07:14 PM||||Thanks guys!||||reg||1
Z||000028||artherd||10-21-2001||10:27 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Capt Fiero:<BR><B>One other question, will these draw more or less current than the standard sealed beam lights that are stock.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Uh, yeah, depending on what bulbs they include, they will probally DOUBLE your power draw...<P>55/65w is standard (and bulbs can be purchased for those housings, a great setup, far supior to stock! you could safely go 65/75w, etc)<P>However, many 'fake hid' bulbs are in the 110/135watt range, which will roughly double your current draw...<P>The Fiero's wiring is marginal at best, and you very much run a real risk of melting the wires with such high wattage bulbs.<P>This will burn your car to the ground.<P>Please Be careful.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.||||reg||3
Z||000029||artherd||10-21-2001||10:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Capt Fiero:<BR><B>One other question, will these draw more or less current than the standard sealed beam lights that are stock.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Uh, yeah, depending on what bulbs they include, they will probally DOUBLE your power draw...<P>55/65w is standard (and bulbs can be purchased for those housings, a great setup, far supior to stock! you could safely go 65/75w, etc)<P>However, many 'fake hid' bulbs are in the 110/135watt range, which will roughly double your current draw...<P>The Fiero's wiring is marginal at best, and you very much run a real risk of melting the wires with such high wattage bulbs.<P>This will burn your car to the ground.<P>Please Be careful.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
